              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#general"} General
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ReferencesMonoidal"} Monoidal case
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            What is known as
            %em left Bousfield localization of model categories
            (
            %a{:href => "#Hirschhorn02"} Hirschhorn (2002), §3.3
            following
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Bousfield75"} Bousfield (1975)
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+model+categories"} localization of model categories
            corresponding to
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+localization"} reflective localization
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+reflection"} Quillen reflection
            inducing a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+sub-%28infinity%2C1%29-category"}
              reflective sub-
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              \-category
            inclusion in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+localization"} associated
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                \-categories
          %p
            Recall that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+localization"} reflective localization
            of a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            at a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            of morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            can be presented as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fractions"} category of fractions
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            with respect to the class of
            = succeed "-local" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            (and, more generally, of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+category"} relative category
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            can be presented as the same underlying category of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            equipped with the larger class of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalences"} weak equivalences
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+morphisms"} local morphisms
          %p
            Here the process of enlarging the class of weak equivalences can be seen as the homotopy coherent analogue of the classical
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fractions"} category of fractions
          %p
            The historically original example is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+spectra"} Bousfield localization of spectra
            \&amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#Bousfield75"}> Bousfield (1975)
            \&amp;rbrack;, but the notion is much more general, as explained above.
          %p
            The existence of Bousfield localizations for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cellular+model+categories"} cellular model categories
            was established in
            %a{:href => "#Hirschhorn02"} Hirschhorn (2002), Ch. 4
            and for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+categories"} combinatorial model categories
            in
            %a{:href => "#Barwick10"} Barwick (2010), Thm. 4.7
            (based on
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "combinatorial+model+category#SmithTheorem"} Smith’s theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+categories"} simplicial model categories
            also in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Lurie"} Lurie (2009), around A.3.7.3
          %h2#left_localization_at_a_class_of_morphisms Left localization at a class of morphisms
          %p
          #LeftLocalization.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+a+model+category"} left localization
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              with respect to a class of morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
              (if it exists)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi S
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \to L_S C
              in the following category:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                  are
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+Quillen+functors"} left Quillen functors
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo →
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to D
                  whose
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+derived+functor"} left derived functor
                  sends elements of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  to weak equivalences in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                  are commutative triangles of left Quillen functors.
            %p
          (
          %a{:href => "#Hirschhorn02"}> Hirschhorn 2002, Def. 3.3.1
          )
          %p
            This definition
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LeftLocalization"}
            immediately implies that left localizations, if they exist, are unique up to a unique isomorphism.
          %p
            The adjective “left” in Def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LeftLocalization"}
            refers to the fact that the localization functor is implemented as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+derived+functor"} left derived functor
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi S
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to L_S C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+localization"} reflective localization
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            functor.
          %p
            Right localizations are defined analogously and generalize
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreflective+localizations"} coreflective localizations
          %h2#local_objects_and_local_equivalences Local objects and local equivalences
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            with a class of morphisms
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %p
            We want to characterize objects in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            that “see elements of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            as weak equivalences”.
          %p
          .num_lemma
            %h6 Lemma
            %p
              In an ordinary category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon A \to B
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              precisely if for all objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              the morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_C(f,X) \colon Hom_C(B,X) \to Hom_C(A,X)
            %p
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              (of sets, i.e., a
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
          %p So we can “test isomorphism by homming them into objects”.
          %p
            More generally, recall the following facts about
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+localizations"} reflective localizations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a category and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is a class of morphisms in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "-local" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in C
            such that for every
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon A\to B
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(B,X)\to C(A,X)
            is an isomorphism. An
            = succeed "-local" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g\colon E\to F
            such that for every
            = succeed "-local" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(F,X)\to C(E,X)
            is an isomorphism. The reflective localization of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            at
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            (if it exists) is defined as an initial object in the category whose objects are left adjoint functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to D
            that send elements of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            to isomorphisms in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            = succeed "-local" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fractions"} category of fractions
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            with respect to
            = succeed "-local" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+localization"} reflective localization
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            at
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %p
            The following definitions offer a completely analogous picture for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                \-local objects and
                = succeed "-local" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              We say that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  an object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  is an
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local object
                  if for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s : A \hookrightarrow B
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  the morphism
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi RMap
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi s
                        %mo ,
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %mi RMap
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi B
                        %mo ,
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi RMap
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} RMap(s,X) : RMap(B,X) \to RMap(A,X)
                %p
                  is a weak equivalence of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi RMap
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} RMap
                  denotes the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+function+complex"} homotopy function complex
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hammock+localization"} hammock localization
              %li
                %p
                  conversely, say that a map
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : A \hookrightarrow B
                  is an
                  = succeed "-local" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  = succeed "-local" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  the morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi RMap
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo ,
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %mi RMap
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi B
                        %mo ,
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi RMap
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        RMap(f,X) : RMap(B,X) \to
                        RMap(A,X)
                  is a weak equivalence of simplicial sets.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Hirschhorn02"}> Hirschhorn 2002, Def. 3.1.4
            )
          %p
            We write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_S
            for the collection of
            = succeed "-local" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              For every weak equivalence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : A \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} B
              between cofibrant objects and every fibrant object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              the map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(f,X) : C(B,X) \to C(A,X)
            %p
              is a weak equivalence of simplicial sets. This is described in detail at
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-categorical+hom-space#EnrichedHomsCofToFib"} enriched homs from cofibrants to fibrants
          %p
          .num_lemma
            %h6 Lemma
            %p
              Every ordinary weak equivalence is also
              = succeed "-local" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi S
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \subset W_S.
            %p
          (
          %a{:href => "#Hirschhorn02"}> Hirschhorn 2002, Prop 3.1.5
          )
          %h2#Definition Left Bousfield localizations
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong (left Bousfield localization)
            %p
              The left Bousfield localization
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi S
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_S C
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %strong
                at a class of morphisms
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is, if it exists, the new model category structure on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              with
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  cofibrations are the same as before,
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi cof
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi L
                                %mi S
                              %mi C
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi cof
                            %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cof_{L_S C } = cof_C
              %li
                %p
                  weak equivalences are
                  = succeed "-local" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %p
            Again, the adjective “left” refers to the fact that the localization is implemented by the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+derived+functor"} left derived functor
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+localizations"} reflective localizations
          %p
            Right Bousfield localizations are defined analogously and generalize
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreflective+localizations"} coreflective localizations
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Any left Bousfield localization of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              at
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is also a left localization of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              at
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          (
          %a{:href => "#Hirschhorn02"}> Hirschhorn 2002, Thm. 3.3.19
          )
          %p In practice, left localizations are always constructed as left Bousfield localizations. Therefore, both notions are used interchangeably.
          %h2#third_definition Third definition
          %p
          #DefinitionOfLeftBousfieldLocalizations.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em left Bousfield localization
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi loc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{loc}
              of a model category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is another model category structure on the same underlying category with the same cofibrations,
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi cof
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mi loc
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi cof
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cof_{C_{loc}} = cof_c
            %p but more weak equivalences
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mi loc
                    %mo ⊃
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi C
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_{C_{loc}} \supset W_C.
            %p
          %p While that’s a very simple definition, it turns out that something interesting happens to the fibrations when we keep the cofibrations fixed and increase the weak equivalences.
          #ImmediateImpiciationsOfLeftBousfieldLocalization.num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p It follows directly that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mi loc
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{loc}
                  has as
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations"} fibrations
                  a sub-class of the fibrations of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi fib
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mi loc
                        %mo =
                        %mi rlp
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi cof
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mi loc
                        %mo ∩
                        %msub
                          %mi W
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mi loc
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi rlp
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi cof
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mi loc
                        %mo ∩
                        %msub
                          %mi W
                          %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi fib
                          %mi C
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        fib_{C_{loc}} = rlp(cof_{C_{loc}} \cap W_{C_{loc}})
                        \\subset rlp(cof_{C_{loc}} \cap W_C) = fib_{C}
                        \\,.
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mi loc
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{loc}
                  has the same
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/acyclic+fibrations"} acyclic fibrations
                  as
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi fib
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mi loc
                        %mo ∩
                        %msub
                          %mi W
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mi loc
                        %mo =
                        %mi rlp
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi cof
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mi loc
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi rlp
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi cof
                          %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi fib
                          %mi C
                        %mo ∩
                        %msub
                          %mi W
                          %mi C
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        fib_{C_{loc}} \cap W_{C_{loc}}
                        \=
                        rlp(cof_{C_{loc}}) = rlp(cof_C) = fib_C \cap W_C
                        \\,.
              %li
                %p on the underlying categories
                %ul
                  %li
                    %p
                      the identity functor
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi Id
                            %mo :
                            %mi C
                            %mo →
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mi loc
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id : C \to C_{loc}
                      preserves cofibrations and weak equivalences
                  %li
                    %p
                      the identity functor
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi Id
                            %mo :
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mi loc
                            %mo →
                            %mi C
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id : C_{loc} \to C
                      preserves fibrations and acyclic fibrations
                %p
                  so that this pair of functors is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mi loc
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mo ←
                        %mi C
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        C_{loc} \stackrel{\leftarrow}{\to} C
                        \\,,
          %p
            and a very special one: With
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo ∘
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\circ
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            on fibrant-cofibrant objects, under left Bousfield localization the fibrant-cofibrant objects of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi loc
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{loc}
            are a subcollection of those of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi loc
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                  %mo ⊂
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo ∘
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (C_{loc})^\circ \subset C^\circ
                  \\,.
          %p
            Moreover, as we shall see, every object in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is weakly equivalent in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi loc
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{loc}
            to one in
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi loc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{loc}
            %em
              reflects into
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi loc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{loc}
            \.
          .standout
            %p
              Bousfield localization is a model category version of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  reflection onto
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+objects"} local objects
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+localization"} reflective localization
          %p
            Indeed, the Quillen adjunction given by a left Bousfield localization under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} passage to the sub-category of fibrant-cofibrant objects
            becomes the inclusion of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-subcategory"} reflective (∞,1)-subcategory
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi loc
                    %mo ∘
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi lex
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo ∘
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  {C_{loc}}^\circ \stackrel{\stackrel{lex}{\leftarrow}}{\hookrightarrow}
                  C^\circ
          %p
            hence of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} localization of an (∞,1)-category
          %p
            Such a localization is determined by the collection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local weak equivalences
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi loc
                    %mo ∘
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {C_{loc}}^\circ
            is the full
            = succeed "-subcategory" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "-local" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %h2#Properties Properties
          %p
            Assume that the left Bousfield localization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi S
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_S C
            of a given model category at a class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            of morphisms in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            exists. Then it has the following properties.
          %h4#fibrants_in__are_the_local_fibrants_in_
            Fibrants in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi S
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_S C
            are the
            = succeed "-local" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The fibrant objects in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi S
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_S C
              are precisely the fibrant objects in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              that are
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              To see this, we modify, if necessary, the set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              in a convenient way without changing the class
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_S
              of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local weak equivalence
            %p
              %strong Lemma
              We may add to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              any set of
              = succeed "-local" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local object
              = succeed "-local" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              without changing
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_S
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  all generating acyclic cofibrations of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi J
                          %mo ⊂
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \subset S
              %li
                %p
                  for every original morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : A \to B
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  and for every
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
                  also the canonical morphism
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi Q
                          %mi f
                        %mo ≔
                        %mi A
                        %mo ⋅
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi n
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                          %mrow
                            %mi A
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mo ∂
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                        %mi B
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mo ∂
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi B
                        %mo ⋅
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi n
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\tilde f
                        \\;\colon\;
                        \\big(
                        Q_f
                        \\coloneqq
                        A \cdot \Delta^n
                        \\coprod_{A \cdot \partial \Delta^n}
                        B \cdot \partial \Delta^n
                        \\big) \to B \cdot \Delta^n
                        \\,,
                %p
                  where
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ⋅
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \cdot \Delta^n
                  etc. denotes the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copower"} tensoring
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  over
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
            %p
              %strong Proof of the Lemma
            %p
              We discuss why these morphisms of the latter type are indeed
              = succeed "-local" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %p
              to see that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde f
              is indeed a cofibration notice that for every commuting diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Q
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∈
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi fib
                                      %mi C
                                    %mo ∩
                                    %msub
                                      %mi W
                                      %mi C
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                            %mo ⋅
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Q_f &amp;\to&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\in \mathrlap{fib_C \cap W_C}}
                    \\\
                    B \cdot \Delta^n
                    \&amp;\to&amp;
                    Y
                    }
            %p we get as components of the top morphism the left square of
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ∂
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi B
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi B
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\partial \Delta^n &amp;\to&amp; C(B,X) &amp;\to&amp; C(B,Y)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\Delta^n &amp;\to&amp; C(A,X) &amp;\to&amp; C(A,Y)
                    }
            %p
              and similarly the components of the bottom morphism consitute a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^n \to C(B,X)
              which by the commutativity of the original square is a lift of the outer diagram here. The top left triangle of this lift in turn gives a square
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ∂
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi B
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %msub
                                    %mi cof
                                    %mi SSet
                                  %mo ∩
                                  %msub
                                    %mi W
                                    %mi SSet
                                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∈
                                %msub
                                  %mi fib
                                  %mi SSet
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\partial \Delta^n &amp;\to&amp; C(B,X)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathllap{\in cof_{SSet} \cap W_{SSet}\quad}}
                    \&amp;&amp; \quad \downarrow^{\in fib_{SSet}}
                    \\\
                    \\Delta^n &amp;\to&amp; C(A,X)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              So this last diagram has a lift
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Delta^n \to C(B,X))
              and this is adjunct to the lift
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \cdot \Delta^n \to X
              of the original lifting problem that we are looking for.
            %p
              Therefore
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mi f
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde f : Q_f \to B \cdot \Delta^n
              is indeed a cofibration.
            %p Notice that in these arguments we made use of
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  = succeed "ing" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power"} power
                  = succeed "ing" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copower"} copower
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicially+enriched+category"} simplicially enriched category
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  over
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
              %li
                %p
                  and of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+bifunctor"} Quillen bifunctor
                  property of the
                  = succeed "ing" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copower"} copower
            %p
              Next, again using the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+bifunctor"} Quillen bifunctor
              property of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copower"} tensoring
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              over
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
              we find that with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              cofibrant in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^n
              being cofibrant in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
              it follows that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \cdot \Delta^n
              is cofibrant; similarly for the other cases. The coproduct of two cofibrant objects is cofibrant because cofibrations are preserved under pushout. Therefore
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_f
              is indeed a cofibrant domain of our cofibration.
            %p
              With
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde f
              being a cofibration, we can check
              = succeed "-locality" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              = succeed "-local" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %p
              So let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a fibrant and
              = succeed "-local" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
              diagram for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_f
              into
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              produces the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mo ∂
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                            %mo ,
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ←
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi W
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mo ∂
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                            %mo ,
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi B
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi fib
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                            %mo ,
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ←
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi W
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi A
                            %mo ⋅
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                              %mrow
                                %mi A
                                %mo ⋅
                                %mo ∂
                                %msup
                                  %mi Δ
                                  %mi n
                            %mi B
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mo ∂
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi W
                            %mo ↖
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↖
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi B
                            %mo ⋅
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    [\partial \Delta^n,[A,X]]
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\in W}{\leftarrow}&amp;
                    [\partial \Delta^n, [B,X]]
                    \\\
                    \\uparrow^{\mathrlap{\in fib}} &amp;&amp;
                    \\uparrow
                    \\\
                    [\Delta^n,[A,X]]
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\in W}{\leftarrow}&amp;
                    [A \cdot \Delta^n \coprod_{A \cdot \partial \Delta^n} B \cdot \partial \Delta^n, X]
                    \\\
                    \&amp;{}_{\in W}\nwarrow&amp;&amp; \nwarrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp;&amp;&amp; [B \cdot \Delta^n, X]
                    }
            %p
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [B,X] \to [A,X]
              is an acyclic Kan fibration by the characterization of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local cofibrations
              and the fact that
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
              is an
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+model+category"} enriched model category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+model+category"} properness
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
              that the bottom horizontal morphism is a weak equivalence, which finally implies by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+with+weak+equivalences"} 2-out-of-3
              that the morphism in question is a weak equivalence.
            %p
              %strong end of the proof of the lemma
            %p
              This shows that we can assume that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              contain the generating acyclic cofibrations and the morphism called
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde f
            %p
              As usual, we say that given a set of morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              and an object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              has the
              %em extension property
              with respect to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              if every diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi S
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\to&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\in S}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    B &amp;\to&amp; {*}
                    }
            %p has a lift.
            %p
              We claim now that the the objects of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              that have the extension property with respect to our set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              are precisely the fibrant and
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local object
            %p
              In one direction, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              that has the extension property with respect to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              it has it in particular with respect to the generating acyclic cofibrations
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \subset S
              and hence is fibrant, and it, in particular, has the extension property with respect to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⋅
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi n
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo ⋅
                          %mo ∂
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi n
                      %mi B
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mo ∂
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                      %mo ⋅
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde f : A \cdot \Delta^n \coprod_{A \cdot \partial \Delta^n} B \cdot \partial \Delta^n \to B \cdot \Delta^n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_f
              a morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mi f
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Q_f \to X
            %p
              consists of two component maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A \cdot \Delta^n \to X)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo ∂
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (B \cdot \partial \Delta^n \to X)
              such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ∂
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi B
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\partial \Delta^n &amp;\to&amp; C(B,X)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\Delta^n &amp;\to&amp; C(A,X)
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p and in terms of this a lift
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Q
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mo ∃
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi B
                            %mo ⋅
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Q_f &amp;\to&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp; \nearrow_{\exists}
                    \\\
                    B \cdot \Delta^n
                    }
            %p consists of a lift
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo ∂
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi B
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mo ∃
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\partial \Delta^n &amp;\to&amp; C(B,X)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;\nearrow_\exists &amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\Delta^n &amp;\to&amp; C(A,X)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo ∂
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\partial \Delta^n \to \Delta^n | n \in \mathbb{N}\}
              are the generating acylic fibrations in the standard
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              with respect to all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde f
              means that all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(s,X) : C(B,X) \to C(A,X)
              are acyclic
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
            %p
              Conversely, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is fibrant and
              = succeed "-local," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              the map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [B,X] \to [A,X]
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SSet
              is an acyclic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
              hence in particular its underlying map of sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_C(B,X) \to Hom_C(A,X)
              is a surjection, so
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              has the extension property.
            %p
              Now every fibrant object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi S
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_S W
              has the extension property with respect to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi cof
                      %mi C
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cof_C \cap W_S
              hence in particular with respect to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msub
                        %mi cof
                        %mi c
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subset cof_c \cap W_S
              = succeed "-local" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %p
              Conversely, if it is
              = succeed "-local" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi cof
                      %mi C
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in cof_C \cap W_S
              the map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [f,X]
              is an acyclic Kan fibration in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
              so that in particular
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_C(f,X)
              is a surjection, which means that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              has the extension property with respect to all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              and is hence fibrant in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mi S
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_S C
          %h4#fibrant_replacement_in___localization_of_objects
            Fibrant replacement in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi S
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_S W
            – localization of objects
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is a small set, we may apply the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to {*}
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            we obtain a functorial factorization componentwise of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi X
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi cell
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mi S
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi inj
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo *
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X \stackrel{\eta_X \in cell(S)\subset W_S}{\to}
                  T X \stackrel{inj(S)}{\to} {*}
                  \\,.
          %p
            We had remarked already in the previous argument that objects with the extension property relative to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi inj
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} inj(S)
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            Therefore
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is in particular a
            %strong fibrant approximation functor
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi S
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_S W
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi η
                    %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_S
            is the weak equivalence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi η
                    %mi S
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ≃
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi W
                            %mi S
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\eta_S : X \stackrel{\simeq_{W_S}}{\to} T X
          %p
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi S
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_S C
            relating an object to its fibrant approximation.
          %p More precisely:
          #DerivedAdjunctionUnitOfLftBousfieldLoclization.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p Let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi loc
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⊥
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi id
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi id
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{C}_{loc}
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{id}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{id}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\bot}
                    \\mathcal{C}
            %p
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
              which exhibits a left
              = succeed "," do
                %span.newWikiWord
                  Bousfield localization of model categories
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} ?
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi loc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{loc}
              admits
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+factorization"} functorial factorization
              (for instance if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi loc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{loc}
              is, then via the
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi fib
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (-) \longrightarrow (-)^{fib}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Then the derived adjunction unit, i.e. the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+unit"} adjunction unit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi η
                      %mi der
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta^{der}
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+pair"} adjoint pair
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functors"} derived functors
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+a+model+category"} homotopy category
              (as discussed there)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi loc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⊥
                      %munder
                        %mo ↪
                        %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Ho(\mathcal{C}_{loc})
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{}{\hookrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\bot}
                    Ho(\mathcal{C})
            %p
              is isomorphic to the image of the fibrant replacement morphism in
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mi loc
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{loc}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi η
                      %mi X
                      %mi der
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mi fib
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\eta^{der}_X
                    \\simeq
                    \\ell(X \to X^{fib})
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi loc
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi loc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell \;\colon\; \mathcal{C}_{loc} \to Ho(\mathcal{C}_{loc})\;
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
              functor (as discussed at
              = succeed ")." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+a+model+category"} homotopy category of a model category
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              First consider the general prescription (from
              = succeed ")" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+a+model+category"} homotopy category of a model category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functors"} derived functors
              by applying the Quillen functors to fibrant (cofibrant) replacements, where we apply the fibrant replacement functorially also to the non-cofibrantly replaced object:
            %p Let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⊥
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi R
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi L
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{C}
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{R}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{L}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\bot}
                    \\mathcal{D}
            %p
              be a general
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
              betwen
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
              which admit
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+factorization"} functorial factorization
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathcal{D}
              be any
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi cof
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} W
                                  %mo ∩
                                  %mi Fib
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X_{cof}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\in \mathrm{W} \cap Fib}}
                    \\\
                    X
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Then apply
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              to this
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi cof
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    L(X_{cof})
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{}
                    \\\
                    L(X)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p Then apply fibrant replacement functorially
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi cof
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi W
                                %mo ∩
                                %mi Cof
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi cof
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi fib
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi W
                                %mo ∩
                                %mi Cof
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi fib
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    L(X_{cof})
                    \&amp;\overset{\in W \cap Cof}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    (L(X_{cof}))^{fib}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{}
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow
                    \\\
                    L(X)
                    \&amp;\underset{\in W \cap Cof}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    (L(X))^{fib}
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Then apply
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi cof
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi L
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi cof
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi fib
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mi L
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi L
                            %mi X
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi fib
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    R L (X_{cof})
                    \&amp;\overset{}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    R (L X_{cof})^{fib}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{}}
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow
                    \\\
                    R L X &amp;\underset{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; R((L X)^{fib})
                    }
            %p
              Finally, precompose with the ordinary
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+unit"} adjunction unit
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi cof
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi η
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi X
                                      %mi cof
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi cof
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mi R
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi j
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi W
                                %mo ∩
                                %mi Cof
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi L
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi cof
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi fib
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi W
                                  %mo ∩
                                  %mi Fib
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi η
                                  %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mi L
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi R
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi L
                            %mi X
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi fib
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X_{cof}
                    \&amp;\overset{\eta_{X_{cof}}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    R L (X_{cof})
                    \&amp;\overset{R (j \in W \cap Cof)}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    R (L X_{cof})^{fib}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\in W \cap Fib}}
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow
                    \\\
                    X
                    \&amp;\underset{\eta_X}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    R L X &amp;\underset{}{\longrightarrow}&amp; R((L X)^{fib})
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Now in the special case that
