                    \\array{
                    A &amp;\overset{f}{\longrightarrow}&amp; X \mathrlap{\in Fib_{loc}}
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{\in W_{loc} \cap Cof}}\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\in Fib}}
                    \\\
                    B &amp;\underset{g}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y \mathrlap{\in Fib_{loc}}
                    }
            %p
              we need to exhibit a lift. (In labeling the arrows we use throughout that
              = succeed ".)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Cof
                        %mi loc
                      %mo =
                      %mi Cof
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cof_{loc} = Cof
            %p
              By assumption of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+factorization"} functorial factorization
              we may factor this diagram as follows:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∈
                                %msub
                                  %mi W
                                  %mi loc
                                %mo ∩
