            %p
              Since it follows that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo ^
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo ^
                      %mo ^
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Fib
                      %mi loc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat A, \widehat{\widehat A} \in Fib_{loc}
              we invoke prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalWeakEquivalencesBetweenLocalObjects"}
              to conclude that the top middle morphism is not just in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi loc
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi Cof
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_{loc} \cap Cof
              but indeed in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi Cof
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \cap Cof
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lifting"} lifting
              in the top right square. Moreover, we also evidently have lifting in the bottom left square.
            .maruku-equation
