            %p Together, these lifts constitute the desired total lift.
          %h4#LocHasToBeSLoc Every Bousfield localization is of this form
          %p
            We have considered two definitions of left Bousfield localization: in the first we just required that cofibrations are kept and weak equivalences are increased. In the second we more specifically took the weak equivalences to be
            = succeed "-local" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %p We now show that every localization in the first sense is indeed of the second kind if we demand that both the original and the localized category are left proper, cofibrantly generated simplicial model categories.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p In the context of left proper, cofibrantly generated simplicial model categories,
            %p
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi loc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{loc}
              a left Bousfield localization of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              (i.e. a structure with the same cofibrations as
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              and more weak equivalences), there is a set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subset Mor(C)
              such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi loc
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi S
                    %mi C
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C_{loc} = L_S C
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_5 Proof
            %p
              We show that choosing
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi J
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mi loc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S = J_{C_{loc}}
              to be the set of generating acyclic cofibrations does the trick.
            %p
              First, the cofibrations of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi loc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{loc}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi S
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_S C
              coincide. Moreover, the acyclic cofibrations of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi S
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_S C
              contain all the acyclic cofibrations of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi loc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{loc}
              because
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi cof
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mi S
                        %mi C
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mi S
                        %mi C
                    %mo =
                    %mi llp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi rlp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi J
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mi S
                        %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi llp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi rlp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi llp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi rlp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi J
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mi loc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    cof_{L_S C} \cap W_{L_S C} = llp(rlp(J_{L_S C}))
                    \\subset llp(rlp(S)) = llp(rlp(J_{C_{loc}}))
                    \\,.
            %p
              It remains to show that, conversely, every acyclic cofibration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi S
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_S C
              is an acyclic cofibration in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi loc
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{loc}
            %p
              Choose a cofibrant replacement for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                            %mo ′
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∈
                                %msub
                                  %mi cof
                                  %mi C
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                            %mo ′
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %msub
                                    %mi W
                                    %mi C
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %msub
                                    %mi W
                                    %mi C
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X' &amp;\stackrel{\in cof_C}{\to}&amp; Y'
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\in W_C}}
                    \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\in W_C}}
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; Y
                    }
            %p
              Then by 2-out-of-3 and since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mi S
                        %mi C
                    %mo ⊃
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_{L_S C} \supset W_C
              the morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ′
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f' : X' \to Y'
              is still an acyclic cofibration on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mi S
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_S C
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi C
                            %mi loc
                      %mo ⊃
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_{C_{loc}} \supset W_C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f'
              is an acyclic cofibration in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi loc
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{loc}
            %p
              To show that it is an acyclic cofibration in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi loc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{loc}
              it suffices to show that for every fibrant object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi loc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z \in C_{loc}
              the morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C(Y',Z) \to C(X',Z)
            %p
              is a trivial fibration. Either by assumption or by the
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/local+object#PropInModCat"} characterization of S-local cofibrations
              this is the case if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
              is
              = succeed "-local" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi loc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{loc}
              and the second follows because
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi J
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi C
                            %mi loc
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S = J_{C_{loc}}
          %h4#FunctorialityOfLocalization Functoriality of localization
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              be categories for which left Bousfield localization exists, and let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mi R
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi L
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (L \dashv R)
                    \:
                    C
                    \\stackrel{\overset{L}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{R}{\to}}
                    D
            %p
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subset Mor(D)
              there is an induced Quillen equivalence of left Bousfield localizations
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mi R
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi L
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mi S
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (L \dashv R)
                    \:
                    C_{L(S)}
                    \\stackrel{\overset{L}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{R}{\to}}
                    D_{S}
                    \\,.
          %p
            This is due to
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Hirschhorn02"} Hirschhorn (2002)
          %h4#further_properties Further properties
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_bousfield_localization_is_indeed_a_localization Proposition (Bousfield localization is indeed a localization)
            %p
              If the left Bousfield localization exists, i.e.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi S
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_S C
              is indeed a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              with the above definitions of cofibrations and weak equivalences, then it is indeed a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+a+model+category"} localization of a model category
              in that there is a
              %em left Quillen functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi S
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    j \colon C \to L_S C
            %p
              (i.e.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              preserves cofibrations and trivial cofibrations and has a
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            %p
              such that the total left
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Ho
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ho
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi S
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    L j \colon Ho C \to Ho L_S C
            %p
              takes the images of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subset Mor(C)
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(C)
              to
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %p
              and every other left Quillen functor with this property factors by a unique left Quillen functor through
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            %p
              Moreover, the identity functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Id
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Id_C
              on the underlying category is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Id
                      %mi C
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi S
                    %mi C
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ←
                    %mi C
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi Id
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Id_C : L_S C \stackrel{\leftarrow }{\to} C : Id_C
            %p (and is itself a localization functor).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_6 Proof
            %p
              The first part is theorem 3.3.19 in
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Hirschhorn02"} Hirschhorn (2002)
          %h2#Existence Existence of localizations for combinatorial model categories
          %p
            We discuss the existence of left Bousfield localization in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model categories
            \&amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#Barwick10"}> Barwick (2010), Prop. 2.2 (Thm. 2.11 in preprint)
            \&amp;rbrack;.
          %p
            A similar existence result is available in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cellular+model+categories"} cellular model categories
            \&amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#Hirschhorn02"}> Hirschhorn (2002)
            \&amp;rbrack;, but for the combinatorial case a somewhat better theory is available.
          %p
            By the corollary to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dugger%27s+theorem"} Dugger's theorem
            on presentations for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+categories"} combinatorial model categories
            we have that every combinatorial model category is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalent
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+model+category"} left proper
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial
            combinatorial model category.
          %p Therefore there is little loss in assuming this extra structure, which the following statement of the theorem does.
          %p
          #ExistenceForLeftProperCombinatorialSimplicialModelCategories.num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+proper+model+category"} left proper
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            %ul
              %li
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi Mor
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subset Mor(C)
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+set"} small set
                of morphisms,
            %p
              then the left Bousfield localization
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi S
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_S C
              does exist as a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model category
            %p Moreover, it satisfies the following conditions:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the fibrant objects of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mi S
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_S C
                  are precisely the
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  that are fibrant in
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mi S
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_S C
                  is itself a left
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+model+category"} proper model category
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mi S
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_S C
                  is itself a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
            %p
          %p
            (Without the assumption or conclusion of simplicial enrichment, this is
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Barwick10"} Barwick (2010), Prop. 2.2 (Thm. 2.11 in preprint)
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Beke00"} Beke (2000), Thm. 1.7, Prop. 1.15 &amp; 1.19
          .proof
            %h6#proof_7 Proof
            %p
              A proof of this making use of
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category#SmithTheorem"} Jeff Smith’s recognition theorem
              for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model categories
              appears as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop. A.3.7.3
              and as theorem 2.11 in
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0708.2067"} Bar07
              and as theorem 4.7 in
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~clarkbar/complete.pdf"} Bar
            %p
              We follow
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.harvard.edu/~clarkbar/complete.pdf"} Bar
              for the proof that the assumptions of Smith’s recognition theorem are satisfied and follow
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop. A.3.7.3
              for the characterization of the fibrant objects. The details are spelled out in the following subsections.
          %h3#prerequisites_for_the_proof Prerequisites for the proof
          %p The proof we give is self-contained, except that it builds on the following notions and facts.
          %h4#small_objects Small objects
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinal+number"} cardinal number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi κ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            is
            %em regular
            if it is not the cardinality of a union of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi κ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lt \kappa
            sets of size
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lt \kappa
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            is a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+set"} directed set
            if all subsets of cardinality
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi κ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lt \kappa
            have a common upper bound. A
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+colimit"} directed colimit
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi lim
                    %mo →
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lim_\to F
            over a functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi J
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : J \to C
          %p
            An object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            in a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+object"} compact object
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(X,-) : C \to C
            commutes with all
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+colimit"} directed colimit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi λ
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mi κ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda \gt \kappa
            every
            = succeed "-compact" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed "-compact." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
          %p
            This means that a morphism from a
            = succeed "-compact" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed "-directed" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
          %p
            An object is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object"} small object
            if it is
            = succeed "-compact" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small
            but possibly non-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+category"} accessible category
            if it has a small sub-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            of generating
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+object"} compact object
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+colimit"} directed colimit
            over such generators.
          %p
            If such a category has all small colimits, it is called a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
          %p
            In particular, in a locally presentable category the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
            for factoring of morphisms applies with respect to every set of morphisms.
          %h4#combinatorial_model_categories Combinatorial model categories
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model category
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
            that is equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated model category
            structure. So in particular there is a set of generating (acyclic) cofibrations that map between
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+objects"} small objects
          %p
            %a{:href => "combinatorial+model+category#SmithTheorem"} Smith’s recognition theorem
            says that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
            has a combinatorial model category structure already if it has weak equivalences and generating cofibrations satisfying a simple condition and if weak equivalences form an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+category"} accessible
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arrow+category"} arrow category
          %p
            %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category#DuggerTheorem"} Dugger’s theorem
            implies that every combinatorial model category is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalent
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+model+category"} left proper
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial
            combinatorial model category.
          %p
            So we may assume without much restriction of generality that we are dealing with the localization of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+model+category"} left proper
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+simplicial+model+category"} combinatorial simplicial model category
          %p
            Since the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
            applies, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model category
            has fibrant- and cofibrant-replacement functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Q
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P,Q : C \to C
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+factorization"}> functorial factorization
            ).
          %p
            By the axioms of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+model+category"} enriched model category
            it follows that the functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi R
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi C
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi SSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{R}Hom_C \coloneqq C(Q(-),P(-)): C^{op} \times C \to SSet
          %p
            takes values in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complexes"} Kan complexes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+hom+space"} derived hom space
            functor of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi R
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R}Hom(X,Y)
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            of maps from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
          %h4#local_objects Local objects
          %p
            An ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi loc
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %mo ←
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi T
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{loc} \stackrel{\stackrel{T}{\leftarrow]}}{\hookrightarrow} C
            is specified by the preimages
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi isos
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S = T^{-1}(isos)
            of the isomorphisms under
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            as the full subcategory on the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local object
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi S
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_C(A \stackrel{s \in S}{\to}B, X)
            are isomorphisms.
          %p
            The analogous statement in the context of model categories uses the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+hom+space"} derived hom space
            functor instead: given a collection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi Mor
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subset Mor(C)
            an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is called an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local object
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi R
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi S
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R}Hom_C(A \stackrel{s \in S}{\to} B, X)
            are weak equivalences.
          %p
            Similarly, the collection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_S
            of morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : E \to F
            such that for all
            = succeed "-local" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi R
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R}Hom_C(f,X)
            is a weak equivalence is called the collection of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local weak equivalence
          %p
            A
            %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/local+object#PropInModCat"} lemma by Lurie
            says that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi S
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \stackrel{s \in S}{\hookrightarrow} B
            a cofibration and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            fibrant,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            = succeed "-local" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(s,X) : C(B,X) \to C(A,X)
            is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} acyclic Kan fibration
            = succeed "-local" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %h4#homotopy_colimits Homotopy (co)limits
          %p
            In an ordinary category, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            diagram is one such that applying
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_C(X,-) : C \to C
            to it produces a limit diagram in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_C(-,X)
          %p
            In a model category, this has an analog with respect to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+hom+space"} derived hom space
            functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi R
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R}Hom_C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy limit
            diagram is one sent by all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi R
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R}Hom_C(-,X)
            to a homotopy limit (…). Similarly for homotopy colimits.
          %p Sometimes ordinary (co)limits in a model category are already also homotopy colimits:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                an
                %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/local+object#PropInModCat"} observation by Barwick
                shows that in a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+model+category"} left proper
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
                ordinary
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
            %li
              %p
                an
                %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category#hocolims"} observation by Dugger
                shows that
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfinite+composition"} transfinite composition
                colimits of length
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                in a combinatorial model category are automatically homotopy colimits for sufficiently large
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi κ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
          %p
            Since these are the two operations under which
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi cell
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi cof
                    %mi c
                  %mo ∩
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cell(cof_c \cap W_C)
            is closed, this facilitates finding this closure given that by the above the elements of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi cof
                    %mi C
                  %mo ∩
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cof_C \cap W_S
            are characterized by their images under
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi R
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{R}Hom_C(-,X)
            for
            = succeed "-local" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h4#size_issues Size issues
          %p
            The following proof uses the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
            several times. In particular, at one point it is applied relative to the collection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            of morphisms at which we localize. It is at this point that we need that assumption that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is indeed a (small)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
          %p
            For the small object argument itself, this requirement comes from the fact that it involves colimits indexed by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is not a set.
          %p
            The collection of
            = succeed "-local" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is. But for
            %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category#SmithTheorem"} Smith’s recognition theorem
            to apply we need to check that the full subcategory of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Arr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Arr(C)
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_S
            is, while not small,
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+category"} accessible
          %p
            To establish this we need two
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/accessible+category#Properties"} properties of accessible categories
          %h3#the_proof_itself The proof itself
          .standout
            %p
              %strong Beginning of the proof
              of the existence of the left Bousfield localization of a left proper combinatorial simplicial model category at a set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              of morphisms.
          %h4#recognition_of_the_combinatorial_model_structure Recognition of the combinatorial model structure
          %p
            Using
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category#SmithTheorem"} Smith’s recognition theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model category
            structure, it is sufficient to
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                exhibit a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                of cofibrations of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mi S
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_S C
                such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi inj
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi I
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊂
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi L
                            %mi S
                          %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} inj(I) \subset W_{L_S C}
                and such that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi cof
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi I
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi L
                            %mi S
                          %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cof(I) \cap W_{L_S C}
                is closed under
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
                and
