              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is already of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi S
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_{S}A
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              a set of just cofibrations.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_8 Proof
            %p
              See
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop. A.3.7.4
            %p
              We demonstrate that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi J
                      %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \coloneqq J_B
              does the trick.
            %p …
          %h3#using_large_cardinal_axioms Using large cardinal axioms
          %p
            If one assumes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+cardinal"} large cardinal
            axioms then the existence of Bousfield localization follows much more generally.
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vop%C4%9Bnka%27s+principle"} Vopěnka's principle
              implies the statement:
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+proper+model+category"} left proper
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model category
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z \in Mor(C)
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
              of
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              %span.newWikiWord
                left Bousfield localization
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} ?
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi Z
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_Z W
              exists.
          %p
            This is theorem 2.3 in (
            %a{:href => "#RosickyTholen"}> RosickyTholen
            ).
          %h2#existence_of_localizations_for_tractable_ennriched_model_categories Existence of localizations for tractable ennriched model categories
          %p
            The above statement is generalized to the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+model+category"} enriched model category
            theory by the following result:
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_existence_of_enriched_bousfield_localization Theorem (existence of enriched Bousfield localization)
            %p Let
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                  be a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tractable+model+category"} tractable
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tractable+model+category"} tractable
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+model+category"} left proper
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi V
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+model+category"} enriched model category
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi Mor
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subset Mor(C)
                  a small set
            %p
              (all with respect to a fixed
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+universe"} Grothendieck universe
            %p
              Then the left enriched Bousfield localization
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi V
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_{S/V} C
              does exist and is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+model+category"} left proper
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tractable+model+category"} tractable
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#Barwick07a"}> Barwick 2007a, theorem 4.46
            ).
          %h2#examples_and_applications Examples and Applications
          %h3#categories_to_which_the_general_existence_theorem_applies Categories to which the general existence theorem applies
          %p
            The following
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            are left
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+model+category"} proper
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cellular+model+category"} cellular
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi Mor
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subset Mor(C)
            the Bousfield localization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi S
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_S C
            does exist.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
                with its standard
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} model structure on topological spaces
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
                with its standard
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
            %li
              %p
                the category of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+smash+product+of+spectra"} symmetric spectra
                in a pointed left-proper cellular model category
            %li
              %p and so on…
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a left
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+model+category"} proper
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"}> simplicial
            )
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cellular+model+category"} cellular model category
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi D
                      %mo ,
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,C]
                for any (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicially+enriched+category"}> simplicial
                )
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                (using the
                = succeed ");" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+model+structure+on+functors"} global model structure on functors
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over+category"} over category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C/s
                for any object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in C
                \.
          %h3#at_derived_idempotent_monads At derived idempotent monads
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield-Friedlander+theorem"} Bousfield-Friedlander theorem
            gives Bousfield localizations at the
            = succeed "-version" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+functor"} derived functor
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+monads"} idempotent monads
          %p See there for more examples of this general construction.
          %h3#localization_of_spectra Localization of spectra
          %p
            see
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+spectra"} Bousfield localization of spectra
          %h3#local_model_structure_on_presheaves Local model structure on presheaves
          %p
            Left Bousfield localization produces the
            %em local
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+homotopical+presheaves"} model structure on homotopical presheaves
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} local model structure on simplicial presheaves
          %h2#relation_to_other_concepts Relation to other concepts
          %h3#LocPresInf
            Locally presentable
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            As described at
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presentable (∞,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
            is presentable precisely if, as an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicially+enriched+category"} simplicially enriched category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+simplicial+model+category"} combinatorial simplicial model category
          %p
            The
            %em proof
            of this proceeds via Bousfield localization, and effectively exhibits Bousfield localization as the procedure that models
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} localization of an (∞,1)-category
            when
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p For notice that
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                a presentable
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
                is one arising as the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} localization
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi C
                      %mo ≃
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mi Funct
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi K
                      %mo ,
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi Grpd
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %msub
                        %mi PSh
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\mathbf{C} \simeq S^{-1} Funct(K,\infty Grpd) = S^{-1}PSh_{(\infty,1)}(K)
              %p
                of an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-presheaves
            %li
              %p
                every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-presheaves
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi PSh
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi K
                      %mo ,
                      %mi SSet
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi inj
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∘
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh_{(\infty,1)}(K)  \simeq ([K,SSet]_{inj})^\circ
                arises as the subcategory of fibrant-cofibrant objects of the global
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            %li
              %p
                in terms of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi K
                      %mo ,
                      %mi SSet
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi inj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [K,SSet]_{inj}
                the prescription for
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} localization as an (∞,1)-category
                and passing to the subcategory of fibrant-cofibrant objects of the Bousfield localization
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi K
                      %mo ,
                      %mi SSet
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi inj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_S [K,SSet]_{inj}
                is literally the same: in both cases one passes to the full subcategory on the
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                = succeed "s." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+object"} local object
          %p
            Moreover, by
            %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category#duggers_theorem_13"} Dugger’s theorem on combinatorial model categories
            every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+simplicial+model+category"} combinatorial simplicial model category
            arises this way.
          %p
            This is the argument of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop A.3.7.6
          %p
            This gives a good conceptual interpretation of Bousfield localization, since the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} localization of an (∞,1)-category
            is nothing but an adjunction
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi C
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi lex
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{C} \stackrel{\stackrel{lex}{\leftarrow}}{\hookrightarrow}
                  \\mathbf{D}
          %p
            that exhibits
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-subcategory"} reflective (∞,1)-subcategory
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{D}
          %p So we find the diagram
          .standout
            %p
              %strong
                Localization of
                = succeed "-presheaf" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Sh
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mn ∞
                                %mo ,
                                %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi K
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ↪
                              %mover
                                %mo ←
                                %mi lex
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi PSh
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mn ∞
                                %mo ,
                                %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi K
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi abstract
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi higher
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi categorical
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi def
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                              %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi Lurie
                            %mo ′
                            %mi s
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi theorem
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %msup
                              %mi K
                              %mi op
                            %mo ,
                            %mi SSet
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                              %mi inj
                              %mi loc
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ∘
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mover
                                %mo ←
                                %mrow
                                  %mi Bousfield
                                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                  %mi loc
                                  %mo .
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %msup
                              %mi K
                              %mi op
                            %mo ,
                            %mi SSet
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                              %mi inj
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ∘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi concrete
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi realization
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Sh_{(\infty,1)}(K)
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\stackrel{lex}{\leftarrow}}{\hookrightarrow}
                    \&amp;
                    PSh_{(\infty,1)}(K)
                    \&amp;&amp;&amp;
                    abstract\;higher\;categorical\;def
                    \\\
                    \\uparrow^{\simeq}
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\uparrow^{\simeq}
                    \&amp;&amp;&amp; Lurie's \;theorem
                    \\\
                    ([K^{op},SSet]_{inj}^{loc})^\circ
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\stackrel{Bousfield\;loc.}{\leftarrow}}
                    {\to}&amp;
                    ([K^{op},SSet]_{inj})^\circ
                    \&amp;&amp;&amp;
                    concrete\;realization
                    }
                    \\,.
          %p
            Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^\circ
            denotes passing to the full
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicially+enriched+category"} simplicially enriched
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
            on the fibrant-cofibrant objects, regarding that as an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-category"} quasi-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^\circ
            also involves taking the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+coherent+nerve"} homotopy coherent nerve
            of this simplicially enriched category.)
          %h3#localization_of_triangulated_categories Localization of triangulated categories
          %p
            There is also a notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+triangulated+categories"} Bousfield localization of triangulated categories
          %p
            Under suitable conditions it should be true that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            a model category whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(C)
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+category"} triangulated category
            the homotopy category of a left Bousfield localization of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is the left Bousfield localization of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(C)
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/a/136517/1291"} this answer on MO
